ESP32-S31: support F-only (no D) RISC-V harts in FPU context switching

The S31 hart is rv32imafc: it has the F extension but not D.  Upstream
assumes F implies D in three places, and __fstate_save/__fstate_restore
use fsd/fld which trap as illegal instructions on this hart.  With this
patch:

  * fpu.S uses fsw/flw for the task fstate context switch.  The fstate
    struct (__riscv_d_ext_state, 32x u64 slots + fcsr) is unchanged, so
    the ptrace and signal ABIs keep their layout; only the low 32 bits
    of each slot carry live data now.
  * cpufeature.c accepts F without D (validate hook + elf_hwcap mask).
  * switch_to.h gates has_fpu() on RISCV_ISA_EXT_F instead of D.

Kernel C is still built with fd stripped from the base ISA
(KBUILD_BASE_ISA), so the compiler never emits FP instructions in the
kernel; the only FP use is this hand-written context switch.

